    "body": "The maintainer looked at the screenshots of PR #1999 on 2026-11-15.\n\nHis words: \"Looking at the screenshots for PR 1999 - the after screenshot looks really nice. The themes should reflect the spacing acomplished in those..\"\n\nThe \"after\" state of PR #1999 is the target for the spacing. Each theme file supplies these values, and the shell reads them from the theme:\n\n| Value | PR #1999 (head `74e980ae7`) | `main` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tab row height (`RIBBON_TAB_H`) | 24 px | 16 px |\n| Gap between the tab row and the cell row (`RIBBON_CELL_TOP_GAP`) | 4 px | 4 px (not named) |\n| Gap between the cell row and the caption row (`CAPTION_GAP`) | 8 px | none |\n| Caption row height (`CAPTION_ROW_H`) | 18 px | none |\n| Gap below the caption row (`RIBBON_BOTTOM_GAP`) | 4 px | none |\n| Ribbon height at default tokens | 88 px | 66 px |\n\nFor the work:\n\n1. Put the five values in `assets/themes/horizon-day.json` and `assets/themes/teal-night.json`, with the numbers of the table as the start values.\n2. The ribbon height is the sum of the rows and the gaps of the active theme plus its cell height. The code has no number of its own.\n3. Take the row layout code and the tests of the branch `issue/1994-ribbon-rows-white-icons` as the base (`ribbon_rows_have_their_own_heights`, `ribbon_text_rows_stack_top_to_bottom`). Change them to read the values from each theme.\n4. The glyph ink comes from the theme too, as the issue body says. The fixed function `glyph_ink` of that branch is not the result.\n5. The PR body has an \"after\" screenshot of each theme, made offscreen. Compare each with the \"after\" screenshot of PR #1999: the tab text, the cells and the captions have the same space.\n\nDone means, in addition to the list in the issue body:\n\n- In each theme the ribbon rows have the heights and the gaps of the table, or larger.\n- A test for each theme pins that the tab text and the caption text fit in their rows.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
